      "The Museums Victoria biology paragraph on the Chalinolobus gouldii page uses the wording “Gould’s Chocolate Wattled Bats”. That sentence is not treated as a Chocolate Wattled Bat (Chalinolobus morio) account. A photo credit naming Alpine National Park is a specimen image locality, not a recommended viewing site. No forearm length is quoted because the opened pages did not give one."
