      "identification": "No Australian Museum species page was found. No Museums Victoria species profile was found (a specimen-search hit was not opened and is not used). The 1992 Australian Museum guide excluded “the five species of the taxonomically chaotic genus Mormopterus” from its external key, so it does not provide a public field identification for this animal under the older genus. AFD current name: Ozimops ridei (Felten, 1964), common name “Ride's Free-tailed Bat”, family MOLOSSIDAE, genus Ozimops Reardon, McKenzie & Adams, 2014, CAVS 1938. Original combination: Tadarida loriae ridei Felten, 1964. Miscellaneous literature name as printed on AFD: “Mormopterus loriae ridei Felton, 1964.” AFD cites Reardon et al. 2014 for reinstatement as a full species. No colour, ear, tail, or forearm description was on the opened AFD page.",
      "origins": "Family Molossidae (AFD breadcrumb). AFD Distribution States: “New South Wales, Queensland, South Australia, Victoria.” IBRA regions listed: Brigalow Belt North (BBN), Brigalow Belt South (BBS), Central Mackay Coast (CMC), Cape York Peninsula (CYP), Desert Uplands (DEU), Darling Riverine Plains (DRP), Einasleigh Uplands (EIU), Murray Darling Depression (MDD), Nandewar (NAN), New England Tablelands (NET), NSW North Coast (NNC), Riverina (RIV), Sydney Basin (SB), South East Coastal Plain (SCP), South East Corner (SEC), South Eastern Highlands (SEH), South Eastern Queensland (SEQ), Wet Tropics (WT). Victorian Volcanic Plain (VVP) is absent. Victorian Midlands (VM) is absent. Holotype locality on AFD: Cairns, Queensland. There is no ecological-descriptors section on the opened page.",
      "habitat": "Not stated on the Australian Faunal Directory page for Ozimops ridei, which gives taxonomy and distribution and no ecological descriptors (https://biodiversity.org.au/afd/taxa/Ozimops_ridei). No Australian Museum or Museums Victoria ecology page was found.",
      "trees": "Not stated on the Australian Faunal Directory page for Ozimops ridei, which gives taxonomy and distribution and no ecological descriptors (https://biodiversity.org.au/afd/taxa/Ozimops_ridei). No Australian Museum or Museums Victoria ecology page was found.",
      "diet": "Not stated on the Australian Faunal Directory page for Ozimops ridei, which gives taxonomy and distribution and no ecological descriptors (https://biodiversity.org.au/afd/taxa/Ozimops_ridei). No Australian Museum or Museums Victoria ecology page was found.",
      "breeding": "Not stated on the Australian Faunal Directory page for Ozimops ridei, which gives taxonomy and distribution and no ecological descriptors (https://biodiversity.org.au/afd/taxa/Ozimops_ridei). No Australian Museum or Museums Victoria ecology page was found.",
      "activity": "Not stated on the Australian Faunal Directory page for Ozimops ridei, which gives taxonomy and distribution and no ecological descriptors (https://biodiversity.org.au/afd/taxa/Ozimops_ridei). No Australian Museum or Museums Victoria ecology page was found.",
      "bestViewing": "Not stated. The opened sources give no viewing method and no field marks. Do not handle. Better Health Channel (https://www.betterhealth.vic.gov.au/health/conditionsandtreatments/Australian-bat-lyssavirus): any bat in Australia can potentially carry and spread Australian bat lyssavirus, including insect-eating microbats. Wash bites, scratches or saliva exposure for at least 15 minutes, use an antiviral antiseptic named on that page, and seek urgent medical care. Only trained, vaccinated people should handle bats. Wildlife Victoria: admire from a distance and treat every bat as if it carries ABLV.",
      "hangouts": "One row, outside 5 km: January 1991, Victorian Biodiversity Atlas, bat trap, count 1, uncertainty 900 m, locality Kings Court, Teesdale, about 5.3 km. Raw name Ozimops ridei. Synonym search Mormopterus ridei returned 0 rows, and the genus Mormopterus facet was empty. The Australian Faunal Directory includes Victoria but its IBRA regions for this species do not include the Victorian Volcanic Plain (https://biodiversity.org.au/afd/taxa/Ozimops_ridei). One 1991 trap with 900 m uncertainty is a weak record. No iNaturalist observation inside 10 km.",
      "threats": "Not stated on the Australian Faunal Directory page for Ozimops ridei, which gives taxonomy and distribution and no ecological descriptors (https://biodiversity.org.au/afd/taxa/Ozimops_ridei). No Australian Museum or Museums Victoria ecology page was found.",
      "conservation": "July 2026 Flora and Fauna Guarantee Threatened List: no mammal entry for Ozimops ridei (https://www.environment.vic.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0028/793801/FFG_Threatened_List_July_2026.pdf). The 28 August 2026 EPBC extract has no row for this scientific name (https://data.gov.au/data/dataset/ae652011-f39e-4c6c-91b8-1dc2d2dfee8f/resource/78401dce-1f40-49d3-92c4-3713d6e34974/download/20260828spcs.csv). Absence of a row is not a SPRAT sentence that says the species is 'Not listed'. EPBC: not stated. FFG Threatened List July 2026: Ozimops ridei and Mormopterus ridei are absent from the Threatened taxa sheet."
