      "identification": "iNaturalist taxon 42165 is Axis porcinus, preferred common name Indochinese Hog Deer. DEECA and the Game Management Authority use Hog Deer for the animal that is excepted from the private-land unprotection order. No Victorian field-description page was opened, and there is no local record to describe. Chital, Axis axis, was checked because the names are sometimes confused. Its ALA facet inside 50 km was also empty.",
      "origins": "Hog deer are one of the four deer species DEECA says are known in Victoria. They are wildlife under the Wildlife Act 1975, not a CaLP established pest. No release history was opened. No occurrence near Inverleigh, or within 50 km of the centre, was returned by ALA or iNaturalist.",
